WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
10 December 1948.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.410
The world is still reeling
from the Second World War.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.940
The United Nations adopts the
Universal Declaration of Human Rights.

4
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:16.270
In the UK today, the Human Rights Act
1998 makes rights like these part of the

5
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.140
law.

6
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:22.040
But why should every person have rights,
and what do they ask of you in return?

7
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.370
In this mission, you'll
see where believers,

8
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.120
and Humanists, think rights come from.

9
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:31.720
Then you'll test what happens when one
person's rights clash with another's.

10
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:35.560
Your mission: explain why every
person should have rights,

11
00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.640
and what those rights ask of you.
